course: dictionary
lesson: 4210
title: Words that rule and control
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The verb govern has three main meanings. To govern a country is to rule it officially, through its leaders and laws. «New Zealand gave women the vote in 1893, before any other self-governing country.» A self-governing country runs its own affairs, so the clue is that it makes its own decisions.
explain: To govern something is to control or decide how it happens. Look for clues such as rules, laws or decide. «Rules govern the game» means the rules decide how the game is played. If you swap in the word control, the sentence still makes sense: the rules control the game.
explain: The third meaning is more formal: to control your feelings. If someone must govern their temper, they must stay calm and not let anger take over. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still fits, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Govern is a verb, and its forms are govern, governs, governed and governing.
fact: «Govern» means to rule a country, state or group officially.
fact: To govern something means to control or decide how it happens, as in rules that govern play.
fact: Laws in science can also govern how things move, such as motion.
fact: In a more formal sense, «govern» means to control your feelings, as in «govern your temper».
exercise: «New Zealand gave women the vote in 1893, before any other self-governing country.» What does self-governing mean? | A country with many islands | *A country that rules itself | A country that has no rules at all
exercise: «Rules govern the game.» What does this mean? | The players must all sing before they start | The game is always cancelled | The rules are written on paper and never used | *The rules decide how the game is played
exercise: Which word means to keep control of your feelings? | *Govern | Gallop | Gather | Giggle
test: A country is governed by | Its weather and its rain | *Its government, the people who rule it | Its oldest tree
test: Mia says, «I must govern my temper.» What is she saying? | She must go to sleep | *She must stay calm and in control of her anger | She must rule the playground | She must buy a new temper
exam: «Laws govern how cars must stop at red lights.» Which meaning of govern fits best? | To run very fast | *To control or decide how something happens | To control your feelings | To rule officially
